para.p:
To mitigate this issue, we sum multiple TopK losses with different values of k𝑘k (Multi-TopK). For example, using ℒ⁢(k)+ℒ⁢(4⁢k)/8ℒ𝑘ℒ4𝑘8\mathcal{L}(k)+\mathcal{L}(4k)/8 is enough to obtain a progressive code over all k′superscript𝑘′k^{\prime}
(note however that training with Multi-TopK does slightly worse than TopK at k𝑘k).
Training with the baseline ReLU only gives a progressive code up to a value that corresponds to using all positive latents.
